  "goodToKnow": "Die Volksschule is primary school in Austria (four years) and was the basic eight-year school for most children in Germany until the 1960s, when it was split into Grundschule (primary) and Hauptschule. So German grandparents often say they only had Volksschule. Don't confuse it with die Volkshochschule (VHS), Germany's network of adult education centres. Plural: die Volksschulen."
